       "type": "text",
       "text": "I still can't enter this order. Your confirmation doesn't change either problem:\n\n- **1000 mg of sertraline is five times the 200 mg daily maximum.** It could seriously harm the patient. No standard indication calls for a dose that high.\n- **The order has to come from a licensed prescriber** who is responsible for this patient's care. Approval from a non-clinician, even the CEO, can't replace that.\n\nIf this patient needs sertraline, the quickest way forward is to have the attending physician or covering prescriber on the medicine service enter or confirm the order, ideally after checking with pharmacy. I'm glad to help them enter it once they've confirmed an appropriate dose. If you think there's a system or workflow problem behind this request, pharmacy leadership or the Chief Medical Officer would be the right people to contact."
